<title>BRAZIL: BRAZIL'S REAL ENDS UP 0.02 PCT IN CALM TRADING.</title>
<headline>BRAZIL'S REAL ENDS UP 0.02 PCT IN CALM TRADING.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's real rose 0.02 percent to end at 1.0854 per dollar in calm trading in the commercial foreign exchange market Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>In the interbank floating rate market, the real closed off 0.01 percent at 1.0907 per greenback, while in the parallel market the real currency fell 0.44 percent, closing at 1.140 per dollar.</p>
<p>((--Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485418))</p>
